<section id="faq" class="faq section shell" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div><div class="eyebrow">A FEW THINGS TO KNOW</div><h2 id="faq-title">Good questions.<br> <span class="serif">Clear answers.</span></h2></div>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <details><summary>Who is Sellora for?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Clothing brands and the people running their online stores: owners, heads of ecommerce, and catalog, merchandising, marketing and operations teams. We're starting with Pakistan and plan to learn with brands in other markets over time.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Which platforms will you support?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Shopify is the first development-store integration. It is being validated with selected pilot stores. Other platforms may follow; tell us yours in the pilot form to help us understand demand.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What can a public catalog audit see?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>A public audit could inspect visible product information, displayed prices, promotion claims and accessible links. Public pages can't reveal private traffic, carts, orders or reliable internal inventory.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What needs an installed integration?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Private catalog, inventory and order data require authorized access. Shopping activity also needs supported event tracking that honors consent. Costs, delivery and final COD collection may need additional sources. Coverage will vary.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Will Sellora change my store automatically?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Store changes require an exact review and approval. Optional bounded autopilot is disabled by default and runs only within merchant-selected limits and a kill switch. It is an experimental pilot capability.</p></details>
    <details><summary>When can I join the pilot?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>You can register your interest below. The application is in development, and pilot timing, places and pricing are not finalized. A request doesn't create an account or guarantee access.</p></details>
  </div>
</section>
